2026-10-09T02:14:06.2869388Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2876809Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2961411Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2967644Z [0m
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2968151Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2968744Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2968920Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2969451Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2969943Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2970162Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2970358Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2970669Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2970915Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2971282Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2971693Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2972042Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2972318Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2972442Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2972618Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2972810Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2973008Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2973303Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2973406Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2973510Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2973626Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2977706Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2978283Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2983677Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2984025Z I will:
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2984194Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2984560Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2984941Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2985292Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2985593Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2985817Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2986052Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2986441Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2986725Z    /root
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2998792Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T02:14:06.2999364Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3007030Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3007613Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3009092Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3009692Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3010226Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3022851Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3023480Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3031045Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T02:14:06.3031578Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
